s), Erode (textiles), and Salem (steel).\n\nRisks. (1) The TNPCB changes its forms. You must maintain the rule set. (2) Unit owners may not pay for software. Mitigate by charging per document, not per month. (3) A well-funded generic compiler could add Tamil Nadu. Mitigate by going deeper into one district than they will ever go.",
